      <section class="info-section">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <h2>Common sed examples</h2>

            <p>
              Useful commands for common Linux text-processing tasks.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="info-grid">
            <article class="info-card">
              <h3>Replace text</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>
                  <code>sed 's/old/new/' file</code> replaces the first match
                  on each line.
                </li>

                <li>
                  <code>sed 's/old/new/g' file</code> replaces all matches.
                </li>

                <li>
                  <code>sed -i.bak 's/old/new/g' file</code> edits with a
                  backup.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <article class="info-card">
              <h3>Delete and print lines</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>
                  <code>sed '/pattern/d' file</code> deletes matching lines.
                </li>

                <li>
                  <code>sed -n '/pattern/p' file</code> prints matching lines.
                </li>

                <li>
                  <code>sed '5,10d' file</code> deletes lines 5 through 10.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <article class="info-card">
              <h3>Safety recommendations</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>
                  Run the command without <code>-i</code> first.
                </li>

                <li>
                  Use <code>-i.bak</code> to create a backup.
                </li>

                <li>
                  Check special characters in regular expressions.
                </li>

                <li>
                  Use a different delimiter when replacing paths.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

